ve_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/deployments","created_at":"2013-05-27T10:30:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T05:34:20Z","pushed_at":"2025-10-10T19:49:23Z","git_url":"git://github.com/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum","homepage":null,"size":1126,"stargazers_count":629,"watchers_count":629,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":132,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":139,"license":{"key":"bsd-3-clause","name":"BSD 3-Clause \"New\" or \"Revised\" License","spdx_id":"BSD-3-Clause","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/bsd-3-clause","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":132,"open_issues":139,"watchers":629,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I spent a good deal of time today working through this problem, and I figured I should document it here. The error becomes apparent when a user tries to flush objects that are versioned, but the session is not being tracked by the versioning_manager. A `KeyError` exception is raised as the session is not in `versioning_manager.units_of_work`.\r\n\r\n[`make_versioned`](https://github.com/kvesteri/sqlalchemy-continuum/blob/712fa5727644e1744db0a4f2e4aac80826442736/sqlalchemy_continuum/__init__.py#L29) by default uses the default session factory for sqlalchemy (`sqlalchemy.orm.session.Session`). This behavior cannot be overridden either – [`versioning_manager.track_session(...)`](https://github.com/kvesteri/sqlalchemy-continuum/blob/712fa5727644e1744db0a4f2e4aac80826442736/sqlalchemy_continuum/__init__.py#L65) is called for whatever value is provided (i.e. `None` is not allowed, as an exception is thrown).\r\n\r\nThis is probably not a good idea, as common practices like dependency-injection break this. An example would be if a user is to generate his own session factory using `sqlalchemy.orm.session.sessionmaker` (as is encouraged).\r\n\r\nAnyway, the solution here is to call `versioning_manager.track_session(my_session_factory)` with the `my_session_factory` the user has generated from `sessionmaker`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/issues/187/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy-continuum/sqlalchemy-continuum/issues/187/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]